WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.282
Read the supplied fictional practice policy before drafting.

00:00:03.282 --> 00:00:06.974
It allows only invented service category and requested action.

00:00:06.974 --> 00:00:11.896
Names, addresses, contact details, account numbers and real customer records are excluded.

00:00:11.896 --> 00:00:15.589
The invented source asks which appointment times are available.

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:20.511
Select appointment inquiry and ask about available times as the two inputs.

00:00:20.511 --> 00:00:23.793
A draft then says your appointment is confirmed.

00:00:23.793 --> 00:00:26.665
That approval is absent from the source.

00:00:26.665 --> 00:00:32.408
The service reviewer removes it and retains the inquiry for review within the practice.

00:00:32.408 --> 00:00:37.741
If a detail is uncertain, stop before input and ask the policy owner.

00:00:37.741 --> 00:00:42.253
Removing a name from a real record would not establish permission.

00:00:42.253 --> 00:00:46.766
Use this example to show the task and approval boundary together.

00:00:46.766 --> 00:00:51.278
Your real project still needs its own approved policy and environment.
